{"boost_definition":"Intel boost_ghz is the ARK Max Turbo Frequency (the headline 'up to' figure). For K-series chips this includes Thermal Velocity Boost / Turbo Boost Max 3.0, so it is higher than the P-core-only Max Turbo (for example i7-13700K: Max Turbo 5.4 GHz, P-core Max Turbo 5.3 GHz). AMD boost_ghz is the Max Boost Clock. e_core_boost_ghz is Intel's E-core turbo figure: Efficient-core Max Turbo Frequency (12th-14th gen), Single E-core Turbo Frequency (Core Ultra desktop), Low Power Efficient-core Max Turbo Frequency (Core Ultra 200V, which has no standard E-cores). A rated boost clock is a spec-sheet maximum, not a guaranteed sustained clock: it depends on thermals, power limits and core count.","coverage":"74 CPUs in v1.0.0: Intel Core 8th-14th gen desktop, Core Ultra 100/200 desktop and mobile, Intel 8th/10th/11th-gen mobile U/G/H; AMD Ryzen 1000-9000 desktop and Ryzen 3000-8000 plus Ryzen AI 300 mobile. NOT included: 12th/13th-gen Intel mobile H/P chips (Intel publishes no per-SKU P-core base frequency for them, so their rows cannot be completed without inference), i3-8100 (no Turbo Boost, so no boost figure exists), i5-14400, i9-11980HK, Ryzen 7 3700U (no verifiable manufacturer page found). A model that is not in the dataset has no rated spec, never a guessed one.","cpus":[{"base_ghz":2.8,"boost_ghz":4.0,"display_name":"Intel Core i5-8400","e_core_boost_ghz":null,"model":"I5-8400","retrieved":"2026-11-14","source_url":"https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/products/compare.html?productIds=126687,134898","vendor":"Intel"},{"base_ghz":3.6,"boost_ghz":4.3,"display_name":"Intel Core i5-8600K","e_core_boost_ghz":null,"model":"I5-8600K","retrieved":"2026-11-14","source_url":"https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/products/compare.html?productIds=%2F126685%2C134896","vendor":"Intel"},{"base_ghz":3.7,"boost_ghz":4.7,"display_name":"Intel Core i7-8700K","e_core_boost_ghz":null,"model":"I7-8700K","retrieved":"2026-11-14","source_url":"https://ark.intel.com/pr